  "notes": "{温|あたた}める means to warm or heat something, particularly food, drinks, or body parts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {温|あたた}まる (intransitive) - to become warm\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {温|あたた}める: to warm objects, food, body ({温|おん} = temperature)\n- {暖|あたた}める: to warm rooms, air, atmosphere ({暖|だん} = warmth)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- スープを{温|あたた}める: to heat up soup\n- {体|からだ}を{温|あたた}める: to warm one's body\n- {手|て}を{温|あたた}める: to warm one's hands\n- お{弁当|べんとう}を{温|あたた}める: to heat up a lunch box\n\nCONVENIENCE STORE PHRASE:\n{温|あたた}めますか？ 'Shall I heat this up?' - commonly asked when buying food at a コンビニ.",
